{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And He charged them concerning the children of Israel.</b> That they should bear their burden and their load, and that they not become angry with them, and that they not curse them. <b>And concerning Pharaoh king of Egypt,</b> that they should conduct themselves with honor toward the king, as our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: not ״פן יפגעך״ was said, but rather (Exodus 10:29) ״פן יפגענו״ — render honor to the sovereign. And so Moses our master, peace be upon him, conducted himself with honor toward him, as it is said (Exodus 11:8): ״ואלה אלי״ — and not ״ואליך״." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> ״ויצום אל בני ישראל״ — He warned them concerning idolatry (ע\"ג), for Israel were worshipping idols in Egypt. And so they interpreted concerning the first man: ״ויצו״ — this is idolatry, as it is said (Hosea 5:11): ״כי הואיל הלך אחרי צו״. And so it is explicit in Ezekiel that Israel were worshipping idols in Egypt, as it is said (Ezekiel 20:7): ״ביום בחרי בישראל ואשא את ידי להם וגו״ — and He said to them: ״איש שקוצי עיניו השליכו ובגלולי מצרים אל תטמאו״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The citation (שם ה) refers back to Exodus, the verse quoted is Exodus 10:29; the prooftext from שם י\"א is Exodus 11:8. The phrases ולא אמר וירדת and the comparison between פן יפגעך / פן יפגענו appear slightly compressed in the source; translated hyper-literally.", 1 "The abbreviation ע\"ג resolved as עבודה זרה (idolatry) based on the prooftexts cited; the Ezekiel quotation is abbreviated mid-verse in the source and translated as abbreviated."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:56:32.844479432Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}